# Task 143-017: E2E Harness (Chain Safety Foundation)

## Approach
1. Create `tests/e2e/chain-safety.e2e.test.ts` — new file with 10+ E2E scenarios for chain safety gate
2. Extend `tests/e2e/sprint-lifecycle.e2e.test.ts` — add chain-related lifecycle test
3. Create `scripts/run-e2e-harness.mjs` — standalone runner for `npm run e2e:chain`

## Chain Safety Gate Logic (simulated)
The chain safety gate runs 5 checks after sprint finalization:
1. doctor PASS
2. tsc --noEmit 0 errors
3. vitest ≥99% pass
4. Sprint cost <$100 (subs mode threshold)
5. NO_GO count <3

PASS → auto-trigger next sprint
FAIL → abort + notify

## Test Scenarios (chain-safety.e2e.test.ts)
1. All 5 checks pass → PASS gate → auto-trigger signal
2. 3+ NO_GO tasks → FAIL gate → abort
3. Cost >$100 → FAIL gate → abort
4. Doctor failure → FAIL gate
5. tsc errors → FAIL gate
6. vitest <99% pass → FAIL gate
7. Exactly 2 NO_GO → still PASS (boundary)
8. Cost exactly $100 → still PASS (boundary)
9. Mixed failures (cost + NO_GO) → FAIL
10. Empty sprint (0 tasks) → PASS (edge case)
11. All NO_GO sprint → FAIL + abort-notify
12. PASS gate returns next sprint trigger info

